{
  "name": "Irresistible Command",
  "type": "spell",
  "img": "modules/titan-vttrpg-compendium/icons/traditions/Thought_Tradition_Icon.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": "<p>You force those around you to follow an order that you give them.</p><p>Choose a thinking creature within <strong>10 spaces</strong>. It must make a <strong>Willpower</strong> check or spend its next action performing a simple command, such as \"kneel, kill them, run away,\" etc.</p><p>Your command can be no more than 3 words long.</p><p>You cannot command a creature to volunteer information in this way, but you can force it to say a specific phrase.</p><p>Creatures automatically resist commands that would bring obvious harm to themselves.</p><p>If the command is for the creature to do something that goes strongly against its character, it has <strong>Advantage</strong> on the check to resist.</p><p>Each extra success increases the number of affected creatures by <strong>+1</strong>.</p>",
